---
name: d3-v6-force-bubble
description: Build D3.js v6 force-directed bubble charts with clustering, collisions, labels, and tooltips.
---

# D3 v6 Force Bubble

## When to use
Use for bubble charts where nodes represent entities sized by a metric, colored by category, and clustered by category using forceX/forceY.

## Setup
- Include D3 v6: `js/d3.v6.min.js` loaded before your visualization script.
- Create an SVG container with width/height and a centered `<g>` group.

## Core pattern
```js
const width = 900;
const height = 520;
const svg = d3.select('#chart')
  .append('svg')
  .attr('viewBox', `0 0 ${width} ${height}`)
  .attr('preserveAspectRatio', 'xMidYMid meet');

const g = svg.append('g');

const color = d3.scaleOrdinal()
  .domain(sectors)
  .range(d3.schemeTableau10);

const r = d3.scaleSqrt()
  .domain([minCap, maxCap])
  .range([12, 55]);

const centers = d3.scalePoint()
  .domain(sectors)
  .range([width * 0.2, width * 0.8]);

const nodes = data.map(d => ({
  ...d,
  radius: d.marketCap ? r(d.marketCap) : 18
}));

const simulation = d3.forceSimulation(nodes)
  .force('x', d3.forceX(d => centers(d.sector)).strength(0.2))
  .force('y', d3.forceY(height / 2).strength(0.2))
  .force('collide', d3.forceCollide(d => d.radius + 1).iterations(2))
  .force('charge', d3.forceManyBody().strength(-2))
  .alphaDecay(0.03);

const node = g.selectAll('g.node')
  .data(nodes, d => d.ticker)
  .enter().append('g')
  .attr('class', 'node');

node.append('circle')
  .attr('r', d => d.radius)
  .attr('fill', d => color(d.sector));

node.append('text')
  .attr('class', 'label')
  .attr('text-anchor', 'middle')
  .attr('dy', '0.35em')
  .text(d => d.ticker);

simulation.on('tick', () => {
  node.attr('transform', d => `translate(${d.x},${d.y})`);
});
```

## Tooltips
Use an absolutely positioned div and update on mousemove.
```js
const tooltip = d3.select('body').append('div')
  .attr('class', 'tooltip')
  .style('opacity', 0);

node.on('mousemove', (event, d) => {
  tooltip.style('opacity', 1)
    .style('left', `${event.pageX + 12}px`)
    .style('top', `${event.pageY + 12}px`)
    .html(`<strong>${d.ticker}</strong><br>${d.name}<br>${d.sector}`);
}).on('mouseleave', () => tooltip.style('opacity', 0));
```

## Notes
- Keep cluster centers reasonably close using a point scale or a small grid.
- Use `forceCollide` to prevent overlap.
- Use `scaleSqrt` for radius to reduce dominance of large values.
EOF"}

