---
name: d3-csv-data-formatting
description: Parse CSV data with D3.js, normalize numeric fields, and format large numbers for display.
---

# D3 CSV Data Formatting

## When to use
Use when loading CSV data that contains numeric fields stored as strings and needs human-readable formatting.

## Load + parse
```js
const parseMarketCap = (value) => {
  if (!value) return null;
  const cleaned = value.replace(/[^0-9.]/g, '');
  return cleaned ? +cleaned : null;
};

const data = await d3.csv('data/stock-descriptions.csv', d => ({
  ticker: d.ticker,
  name: d.name,
  sector: d.sector || 'Unknown',
  marketCap: parseMarketCap(d.marketCap),
  country: d.country || null,
  website: d.website || null
}));
```

## Human-readable formatting
```js
const formatCap = (value) => {
  if (value == null) return 'N/A';
  const fmt = d3.format('~s');
  const out = fmt(value);
  return out.replace('G', 'B');
};
```

## Notes
- ETFs may have null market cap; handle uniformly in size/formatting.
- Use null for missing values and check before tooltip rendering.
EOF"}

