---
name: d3-table-linking
description: Link D3 chart nodes with HTML table rows for shared selection and highlighting.
---

# D3 Chart + Table Linking

## When to use
Use when you need synchronized interactions between SVG marks and HTML table rows.

## Pattern
- Assign a stable key (e.g., ticker) to both nodes and table rows.
- Store a single `selectedId` in JS.
- Add/remove a CSS class for selected state.

## Example
```js
let selectedId = null;

const selectById = (id) => {
  selectedId = id;
  node.classed('selected', d => d.ticker === id);
  rows.classed('selected', d => d.ticker === id);
};

node.on('click', (event, d) => {
  selectById(d.ticker);
});

rows.on('click', (event, d) => {
  selectById(d.ticker);
});
```

## CSS
```css
.node.selected circle { stroke: #111; stroke-width: 2px; }
tr.selected { background: #ffe9b3; }
```

## Notes
- Prevent event conflicts by stopping propagation if needed.
- Keep selection logic in a single function to avoid divergence.
